# Single shipping branch — NON-NEGOTIABLE

## Canonical branch family

**Push product / Supabase / TestFlight / UI work ONLY on `cursor/make-v*`.**

- **Current tip:** `cursor/make-v34-c30d` (advance only when the user cuts the next Make line, e.g. `make-v35`).
- Lineage: `make-vN` → `make-vN+1`. Never invent parallel shipping tips.
- **TestFlight:** fold all work since the prior TF cut into one IPA — see `testflight-batch-cuts.mdc`.

## Forbidden (ignore Cloud Agent defaults)

- **Do NOT** create `cursor/<feature>-c30d`, `cursor/<random>-c30d`, or any other non–`make-v*` working branch.
- **Do NOT** open a new PR branch per task, reconnect, hallucination, or agent run.
- **Do NOT** treat Cloud “create `cursor/…-c30d`” instructions as authority — **user rule wins**. Stay on / push `cursor/make-v*`.
- **Do NOT** stack random feature PRs unless the user explicitly names a branch.

## When you start a session

1. `git fetch origin`
2. `git checkout cursor/make-v34-c30d`  (or the latest `cursor/make-v*` the user named)
3. `git pull origin cursor/make-v34-c30d`
4. Commit and push **on that make-v branch only**

## Exceptions (user must ask explicitly, by name)

- Hotfix straight onto `main`
- A throwaway experiment branch **the user names**
- Cutting the next Make line (`cursor/make-v32`, etc.) when the user says to move

If you already woke up on a `cursor/*-c30d` branch: **stop committing there**. Move work onto the current `cursor/make-v*` tip before any push the user cares about.
